       that ignores the "watermark" field and acts as if  a  wakeup_event  was
       chosen if the union has a nonzero value in it.

       From  Linux 2.6.31 to Linux 3.4, the PPEERRFF__IIOOCC__FFLLAAGG__GGRROOUUPP ioctl argument
       was broken and would repeatedly operate on the event  specified  rather
       than iterating across all sibling events in a group.

       From  Linux  3.4 to Linux 3.11, the mmap _c_a_p___u_s_r___r_d_p_m_c and _c_a_p___u_s_r___t_i_m_e
       bits mapped to the same location.   Code  should  migrate  to  the  new
       _c_a_p___u_s_e_r___r_d_p_m_c and _c_a_p___u_s_e_r___t_i_m_e fields instead.

